				 <column name="text"
								 value="&lt;h1&gt;Headings. Helpers and nodes config&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;What if you do not have a registered &lt;code&gt;&lt;strong&gt;lexical&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/code&gt; command? Let's try to convert the paragraph element (lexical's default node) into the Header Node without using the&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are no pre-defined commands for converting some Node to the Heading Node, so here we:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Calling &lt;code&gt;editor.update&lt;/code&gt; function that expects a callback as an argument;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;$getSelection&lt;/code&gt; helper for getting selected node;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Checking that it is a &lt;code&gt;RangeSelection&lt;/code&gt; type by using &lt;code&gt;$isRangeSelection&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;4. &lt;code&gt;$setBlocksType&lt;/code&gt; as new &lt;code&gt;$createHeadingNode&lt;/code&gt; (h1,h2,h3);&lt;/p&gt;"/>
				 <column name="last_edit_date" value="1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 GMT"/>
